6","asset_class":"Private equity","deal_type":"Take-private","value_creation_plan":"Apollo said the transaction, with key financial institutions, will strengthen NSG's financial foundation to accelerate investments in its people and technology, drawing on Apollo's prior investment experience in glass, automotive and manufacturing to build a more robust and sustainable business.","value_creation_source_url":"https://ir.apollo.com/news-events/press-releases/detail/653/apollo-funds-announce-completion-of-acquisition-of-nippon","notes":"Apollo Asia Pacific Private Equity lead partner Tetsuji Okamoto. New management structure launched at closing."}},{"name":"BauWatch","website":"https://www.bauwatch.com/","description":"BauWatch is the European market leader in technology-enabled remote video surveillance, safeguarding construction projects and infrastructure such as power plants, substations and renewable energy assets through an integrated platform of remote video surveillance, AI-enabled monitoring and 24/7 alarm response.","sector":"Business Services","subsector":"Mobile security / remote video surveillance","country":"Netherlands","business_model":"B2B security-as-a-service (surveillance systems with monitoring and alarm response; highly recurring revenues on a well-invested asset base)","revenue":153000000,"revenue_currency":"EUR","revenue_period":"FY2025","leaders":[{"role":"ceo","name":"Al Ghelani","title":"CEO","source_url":"https://www.cvc.com/media/news/2026/carlyle-and-cvc-dif-agree-to-acquire-bauwatch-from-haniel/","source_kind":"sponsor","evidence":"Al Ghelani, CEO of BauWatch, said: \"Since Haniel's acquisition of BauWatch, we have grown into the European market leader in our industry.\""},{"role":"managing_director","name":"Klaus Maskort","title":"Geschäftsführer, BauWatch Projekt Service GmbH (German subsidiary)","source_url":"https://www.bauwatch.com/de-de/impressum","source_kind":"company","evidence":"BauWatch Projekt Service GmbH ... Vertretungsberechtigte Geschäftsführer: Shital Ghelani, Klaus Maskort, Frederik Nette"},{"role":"managing_director","name":"Frederik Nette","title":"Geschäftsführer, BauWatch Projekt Service GmbH (German subsidiary)","source_url":"https://www.bauwatch.com/de-de/impressum","source_kind":"company","evidence":"BauWatch Projekt Service GmbH ... Vertretungsberechtigte Geschäftsführer: Shital Ghelani, Klaus Maskort, Frederik Nette"}],"notes":"Headquartered in Apeldoorn, the Netherlands; active in 12 European markets with more than 15,000 active surveillance systems and over 50,000 completed projects. Revenue grew from EUR 59 million (at Haniel's 2021 acquisition) to EUR 153 million in 2025 per the sellers' and buyers' joint release. Reuters (2026-09-17) reported the deal values BauWatch at around EUR 1 billion according to two sources, with Carlyle and CVC DIF taking 45% each and Haniel keeping 10%; closing expected Q1 2027. Founded about 17 years ago (Reuters; site says 'over 17 years of experience'), so no exact founded year is recorded. Only country-specific contact emails are published (e.g. info-uk@, info-DE@), so none is recorded. Group CFO not found. The Carlyle press page returned 403.","sources":{"description":{"url":"https://www.cvc.com/media/news/2026/carlyle-and-cvc-dif-agree-to-acquire-bauwatch-from-haniel/","name":"CVC","kind":"sponsor","as_of":"2026-09-17","evidence":"BauWatch helps safeguard large-scale construction projects and important infrastructure such as power plants and substations, renewable energy assets and other key assets through an integrated platform combining remote video surveillance, AI-enabled monitoring and 24/7 alarm response services."},"revenue":{"url":"https://www.cvc.com/media/news/2026/carlyle-and-cvc-dif-agree-to-acquire-bauwatch-from-haniel/","name":"CVC","kind":"sponsor","as_of":"2026-09-17","evidence":"Under Haniel's ownership, revenue grew from €59 million to €153 million in 2025, alongside consistently improving profitability."},"country":{"url":"https://www.cvc.com/media/news/2026/carlyle-and-cvc-dif-agree-to-acquire-bauwatch-from-haniel/","name":"CVC","kind":"sponsor","as_of":"2026-09-17","evidence":"Headquartered in Apeldoorn, the Netherlands"},"business_model":{"url":"https://www.cvc.com/media/news/2026/carlyle-and-cvc-dif-agree-to-acquire-bauwatch-from-haniel/","name":"CVC","kind":"sponsor","as_of":"2026-09-17","evidence":"a key service, a scalable platform and highly recurring revenues underpinned by a substantial, well-invested asset base"}},"holding":{"sponsor":"The Carlyle Group","status_note":"Agreed 2026-09-17 to acquire BauWatch from Haniel with CVC DIF (45% each per Reuters; Haniel retains 10%); closing expected Q1 2027","asset_class":"Private equity","deal_type":"Buyout","value_creation_plan":"Carlyle and CVC DIF will support BauWatch's next phase of growth through continued investment in innovation, enhancing its product portfolio and accelerating international expansion; Carlyle aims to strengthen its leadership position and support its international expansion.","value_creation_source_url":"https://www.cvc.com/media/news/2026/carlyle-and-cvc-dif-agree-to-acquire-bauwatch-from-haniel/","notes":"Equity from the Carlyle Europe Partners platform (European mid-market). Pending at 2026-10-01, so status is left blank. Carlyle's own release page returned 403; the joint release on cvc.com was used."}},{"name":"BauWatch","website":"https://www.bauwatch.com/","description":"BauWatch is the European market leader in technology-enabled remote video surveillance, safeguarding construction projects and infrastructure such as power plants, substations and renewable energy assets through an integrated platform of remote video surveillance, AI-enabled monitoring and 24/7 alarm response.","sector":"Business Services","subsector":"Mobile security / remote video surveillance","country":"Netherlands","business_model":"B2B security-as-a-service (surveillance systems with monitoring and alarm response; highly 